From 824b716b467db9c421510902bd24bc6d3d0b1368 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:09:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hexagonrpcd: answer a request it cannot serve, and keep
 listening

A request the listener cannot serve (an unsupported method, unexpected
buffers) set its error but ended the listener loop without sending it.
hexagonrpcd then exited and the remote caller waited for good. On the
KONKR Pocket FIT Elite the ADSP sensors process asks for apps_std method
36 at start-up; left unanswered, it keeps the ADSP from ever sleeping, so
the SoC never reaches CX or DDR collapse in suspend. Answer such a request
with its error and no output buffers, and go on.

The returned and decoded buffers are also reset once freed, so a failed
request does not hand the next reply a freed buffer.
---
 hexagonrpcd/listener.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hexagonrpcd/listener.c b/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
index a6a592e..c1e7f80 100644
--- a/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
@@ -384,15 +384,27 @@ int run_fastrpc_listener(int fd,
 
 		if (returned != NULL)
 			iobuf_free(n_outbufs, returned);
+		returned = NULL;
 
 		ret = invoke_requested_procedure(n_ifaces, ifaces,
 						 handle, sc, &result,
 						 decoded, &returned);
-		if (ret)
-			break;
 
 		if (decoded != NULL)
 			iobuf_free(REMOTE_SCALARS_INBUFS(sc), decoded);
+		decoded = NULL;
+
+		/*
+		 * A request that can't be served (an unsupported method, bad
+		 * buffers) is answered with its error and no output, and the
+		 * listener goes on. Leaving it unanswered leaves the remote
+		 * caller waiting for good: the sensors process keeps the ADSP
+		 * from ever sleeping.
+		 */
+		if (ret) {
+			sc = REMOTE_SCALARS_MAKE(0, 0, 0);
+			ret = 0;
+		}
 
 		n_outbufs = REMOTE_SCALARS_OUTBUFS(sc);
 	}
-- 
